cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite it as below, together with the paper it builds on."
title: "Completing broken meshes with generalized winding numbers, cap fairing and symmetry completion"
authors:
  - family-names: Allara
    given-names: Lucas
    affiliation: "Universidad Torcuato Di Tella"
date-released: 2026-11-21
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Lucas-Allara/Broken-mesh-completion"
abstract: >-
  An implementation in C++ of "Robust Inside-Outside Segmentation using Generalized Winding
  Numbers" (Jacobson, Kavan and Sorkine-Hornung, SIGGRAPH 2013), with a conforming
  tetrahedralization, a graph cut and the optional constraints of the paper, extended with two
  stages that give shape to the holes, namely a tri-Laplacian fairing of the caps that keeps the
  input fixed and a completion that mirrors the input across its symmetry plane.
keywords:
  - generalized winding numbers
  - inside-outside segmentation
  - mesh repair
  - hole filling
  - graph cut
  - fairing
  - symmetry
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Robust Inside-Outside Segmentation using Generalized Winding Numbers"
    authors:
      - family-names: Jacobson
        given-names: Alec
      - family-names: Kavan
        given-names: Ladislav
      - family-names: Sorkine-Hornung
        given-names: Olga
    journal: "ACM Transactions on Graphics"
    volume: 32
    issue: 4
    year: 2013
    doi: 10.1145/2461912.2461916
